05:57.450 --> 06:00.630
Pretend that I've been working on that all morning.

06:00.630 --> 06:04.290
Okay? So that looks fine enough, right?

06:04.290 --> 06:06.690
And the good news is that if I wanna share this,

06:06.690 --> 06:08.550
if I'm maybe I'm not done,

06:08.550 --> 06:09.750
but I wanna share it with somebody

06:09.750 --> 06:12.660
and push it up to GitHub, I can push this branch up

06:12.660 --> 06:14.010
at any point.

06:14.010 --> 06:16.140
It doesn't matter what other people have done.

06:16.140 --> 06:18.840
Unlike with our first workflow where I couldn't push

06:18.840 --> 06:21.570
anything up until I had pulled down changes to main or

06:21.570 --> 06:23.790
to Master and I had to merge.

06:23.790 --> 06:27.630
And that process repeated anytime anybody pushed new changes

06:27.630 --> 06:31.530
up to GitHub, everyone else has to pull them down and merge

06:31.530 --> 06:32.700
before they can push.

06:32.700 --> 06:34.290
But that's not an issue here.

06:34.290 --> 06:39.060
So now I can push my branch up if I add those changes.

06:39.060 --> 06:43.740
So git add index, git commit, add pricing table.

06:43.740 --> 06:45.150
I'll just go with that.

06:45.150 --> 06:47.610
Okay? And now I can push that branch up,

06:47.610 --> 06:49.900
git push origin pricing table

06:52.530 --> 06:54.047
And we'll go back to GitHub.

06:56.007 --> 06:58.020
And now we have two branches up here

06:58.020 --> 07:00.450
navbar and pricing table.

07:00.450 --> 07:02.910
Okay? So I'm not necessarily suggesting

07:02.910 --> 07:04.920
that every time you make a feature branch

07:04.920 --> 07:06.870
you need to push it up to GitHub.

07:06.870 --> 07:09.540
A lot of the time you won't do that

07:09.540 --> 07:11.190
unless you have a particular reason

07:11.190 --> 07:13.710
and you need to share that feature branch with somebody.

07:13.710 --> 07:16.770
But often if you look at an organization's repositories

07:16.770 --> 07:18.600
they're not going to have thousands

07:18.600 --> 07:20.280
and thousands of branches even

07:20.280 --> 07:22.740
though there have been thousands of feature branches

07:22.740 --> 07:25.950
over the probably a month or a couple of months at least.

07:25.950 --> 07:29.340
There's just tons and tons of new branches all the time.

07:29.340 --> 07:30.840
We don't push them all to GitHub.

07:30.840 --> 07:32.130
If we do, we remove them.

07:32.130 --> 07:33.540
But also just a lot of the time

07:33.540 --> 07:35.220
you don't need to push them up to GitHub

07:35.220 --> 07:39.240
you will merge them in to master or to main at some point

07:39.240 --> 07:41.490
and then just delete the branch when you're done.

07:41.490 --> 07:43.170
So they don't need to stay around

07:43.170 --> 07:45.060
if you end up merging that stuff in.

